/-! ## The `KFlatBaseChangeData` -> `DerivedBaseChangeData` rename

The 160 records excluded above are not declarations #1416 deleted. They are
declarations it RENAMED, and the audit slice lost them instead of following the
rename: its own log line is "refactor(families): route API through derived
base-change data".

Every one of the 160 sits under
`SchemeBaseChange.KFlatBaseChangeData`, and rewriting that one component to
`DerivedBaseChangeData` reproduces the names `Audit completeness` reports as
NEW and unaudited -- checked against all ten sampled from its output, matched
ten for ten. So the repair is the rename, not a re-derivation.

    AlgebraicGeometry     6069 public,  5189 audited,   880 missing (ceiling 748)
    ::error:: 132 NEW unaudited public declaration(s) absent from the baseline

160 candidates against 132 reported: the surplus is names the refactor dropped
outright as well as renaming. The elaborator filters them -- a record naming
nothing is an `Unknown constant` error and this slice fails to run -- so the
residue is removed in a follow-up pass rather than guessed at here. That is the
same loop that closed the 380 above, and it converges because the build, not a
grep, decides membership.
-/

